              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "CLAUDE.md's session-grouping paragraph still describes the in-memory cache this task deleted",
              "failure": "A contributor or agent reads CLAUDE.md:210 (\"caching the guess in-memory (into m.sessions ...)\") and writes code reading a derived directory off tmux.Session.Dir, reintroducing the conflation the spec forbids. Noticed only as the user-visible symptom: a session becoming findable (or showing a path) after an s regroup that it did not a moment earlier, with no test failing.",
              "detail": "Claim falsified by internal/tui/model.go:1104-1111 (applySessions nils m.derivedDirs) and internal/tui/model.go:1164-1186 (resolveDerivedDirs stores into the map, never into m.sessions). The same paragraph's internal/tui row at CLAUDE.md:67 stays true. Wants one edit at the phase/feature boundary once 1-2 and the directory column land.",
              "files": [
                "CLAUDE.md",
                "internal/tui/model.go",
                "internal/tui/grouping.go"
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "open-with-forced-filter-1-4",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "A classification fixture still uses a single-segment absolute positional, which stops meaning what its name says once the sigil becomes a picker invocation",
              "failure": "At task 1-7 the sigil becomes a picker invocation, so TestShouldRunConcurrentBootstrap_IssuesNoProbe's row labelled \"direct-path open\" would exercise the sigil branch of the decider while claiming to cover the direct-path one. The table would then have no case covering a genuine direct-path positional, so a later change that made the decider issue a tmux round-trip on that branch would pass the suite and be noticed only as a stalled cold-path portal open ~/dir in the field.",
              "detail": "cmd/concurrent_bootstrap_gate_test.go:175 — {\"direct-path open\", openProbeCmd(), []string{\"/dir\"}}. Inert today (isTUIPath, cmd/root.go:168-170, keys on argument count and never consults the resolver). Its siblings in the same file already use ~/dir (:36, :127), so the fix is one word. The other two open <abs path> fixtures (cmd/open_test.go:83, cmd/version_guard_test.go:42) are already multi-segment.",
              "files": [
                "cmd/concurrent_bootstrap_gate_test.go"
              ]
            }
          ],
